[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Internal"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type-only property to carry the inferred data type."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is never set at runtime - it only exists for TypeScript type inference.\nAllows the SDK to know what type to expect when parsing the response."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"json-schema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"json_schema?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional json_schema?: object;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1007","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1007"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JSON schema specification (required when type is \"json_schema\")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defines the exact structure the model's output must conform to.\nOpenAI's structured outputs will guarantee the output matches this schema."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"description","children":[{"type":"text","value":"description?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional description?: string;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional description of what the schema represents."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Helps document the purpose of this structured output."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"\"User profile information including name, email, and preferences\"","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"name","children":[{"type":"text","value":"name"}]},{"type":"code","value":"name: string;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unique name for the schema."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Used to identify the schema in logs and debugging.\nShould be descriptive (e.g., \"user_profile\", \"search_results\")."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"schema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"schema"}]},{"type":"code","value":"schema: Record<string, any>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JSON Schema definition for the expected output structure."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Must be a valid JSON Schema (draft 2020-12 or compatible).\nThe model's output will be validated against this schema."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"see-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"https://json-schema.org/"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"example-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n     *   type: \"object\",\n     *   properties: {\n     *     name: { type: \"string\" },\n     *     age: { type: \"number\" },\n     *     email: { type: \"string\", format: \"email\" }\n     *   },\n     *   required: [\"name\", \"email\"],\n     *   additionalProperties: false\n     * }","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"strict","children":[{"type":"text","value":"strict?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional strict?: boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether to enforce strict schema validation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When true (recommended), the model guarantees output will match the schema exactly.\nWhen false, the model will \"best effort\" match the schema."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default: true (for providers that support it)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"see-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/structured-outputs#strict-mode"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"type","children":[{"type":"text","value":"type"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type: \"json_object\" | \"json_schema\";","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L999","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:999"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type of structured output."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"json_object\": Forces the model to output valid JSON (any structure)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"json_schema\": Validates output against a provided JSON Schema (strict structure)"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"see-4","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/chat/create#chat-create-response_format"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"see","text":"See","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tdata","text":"TData","level":3},{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2},{"id":"data","text":"__data?","level":3},{"id":"json-schema","text":"json_schema?","level":3},{"id":"description","text":"description?","level":4},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":5},{"id":"name","text":"name","level":4},{"id":"schema","text":"schema","level":4},{"id":"see-2","text":"See","level":5},{"id":"example-2","text":"Example","level":5},{"id":"strict","text":"strict?","level":4},{"id":"see-3","text":"See","level":5},{"id":"type","text":"type","level":3},{"id":"see-4","text":"See","level":4}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:990](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L990)\n\nStructured output format specification.\n\nConstrains the model's output to match a specific JSON structure.\nUseful for extracting structured data, form filling, or ensuring consistent response formats.\n\n## See\n\n - https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/structured-outputs\n - https://sdk.vercel.ai/docs/ai-sdk-core/structured-outputs\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` = `any`\n\nTypeScript type of the expected data structure (for type safety)\n\n## Properties\n\n### \\_\\_data?\n\n```ts\noptional __data?: TData;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1068](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1068)\n\n**`Internal`**\n\nType-only property to carry the inferred data type.\n\nThis is never set at runtime - it only exists for TypeScript type inference.\nAllows the SDK to know what type to expect when parsing the response.\n\n***\n\n### json\\_schema?\n\n```ts\noptional json_schema?: object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1007](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1007)\n\nJSON schema specification (required when type is \"json_schema\").\n\nDefines the exact structure the model's output must conform to.\nOpenAI's structured outputs will guarantee the output matches this schema.\n\n#### description?\n\n```ts\noptional description?: string;\n```\n\nOptional description of what the schema represents.\n\nHelps document the purpose of this structured output.\n\n##### Example\n\n```ts\n\"User profile information including name, email, and preferences\"\n```\n\n#### name\n\n```ts\nname: string;\n```\n\nUnique name for the schema.\n\nUsed to identify the schema in logs and debugging.\nShould be descriptive (e.g., \"user_profile\", \"search_results\").\n\n#### schema\n\n```ts\nschema: Record<string, any>;\n```\n\nJSON Schema definition for the expected output structure.\n\nMust be a valid JSON Schema (draft 2020-12 or compatible).\nThe model's output will be validated against this schema.\n\n##### See\n\nhttps://json-schema.org/\n\n##### Example\n\n```ts\n{\n     *   type: \"object\",\n     *   properties: {\n     *     name: { type: \"string\" },\n     *     age: { type: \"number\" },\n     *     email: { type: \"string\", format: \"email\" }\n     *   },\n     *   required: [\"name\", \"email\"],\n     *   additionalProperties: false\n     * }\n```\n\n#### strict?\n\n```ts\noptional strict?: boolean;\n```\n\nWhether to enforce strict schema validation.\n\nWhen true (recommended), the model guarantees output will match the schema exactly.\nWhen false, the model will \"best effort\" match the schema.\n\nDefault: true (for providers that support it)\n\n##### See\n\nhttps://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/structured-outputs#strict-mode\n\n***\n\n### type\n\n```ts\ntype: \"json_object\" | \"json_schema\";\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:999](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L999)\n\nType of structured output.\n\n- \"json_object\": Forces the model to output valid JSON (any structure)\n- \"json_schema\": Validates output against a provided JSON Schema (strict structure)\n\n#### See\n\nhttps://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/chat/create#chat-create-response_format\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: ResponseFormat\ntitle: ResponseFormat\n---\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:990](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L990)\n\nStructured output format specification.\n\nConstrains the model's output to match a specific JSON structure.\nUseful for extracting structured data, form filling, or ensuring consistent response formats.\n\n## See\n\n - https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/structured-outputs\n - https://sdk.vercel.ai/docs/ai-sdk-core/structured-outputs\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` = `any`\n\nTypeScript type of the expected data structure (for type safety)\n\n## Properties\n\n### \\_\\_data?\n\n```ts\noptional __data?: TData;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1068](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1068)\n\n**`Internal`**\n\nType-only property to carry the inferred data type.\n\nThis is never set at runtime - it only exists for TypeScript type inference.\nAllows the SDK to know what type to expect when parsing the response.\n\n***\n\n### json\\_schema?\n\n```ts\noptional json_schema?: object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1007](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1007)\n\nJSON schema specification (required when type is \"json_schema\").\n\nDefines the exact structure the model's output must conform to.\nOpenAI's structured outputs will guarantee the output matches this schema.\n\n#### description?\n\n```ts\noptional description?: string;\n```\n\nOptional description of what the schema represents.\n\nHelps document the purpose of this structured output.\n\n##### Example\n\n```ts\n\"User profile information including name, email, and preferences\"\n```\n\n#### name\n\n```ts\nname: string;\n```\n\nUnique name for the schema.\n\nUsed to identify the schema in logs and debugging.\nShould be descriptive (e.g., \"user_profile\", \"search_results\").\n\n#### schema\n\n```ts\nschema: Record<string, any>;\n```\n\nJSON Schema definition for the expected output structure.\n\nMust be a valid JSON Schema (draft 2020-12 or compatible).\nThe model's output will be validated against this schema.\n\n##### See\n\nhttps://json-schema.org/\n\n##### Example\n\n```ts\n{\n     *   type: \"object\",\n     *   properties: {\n     *     name: { type: \"string\" },\n     *     age: { type: \"number\" },\n     *     email: { type: \"string\", format: \"email\" }\n     *   },\n     *   required: [\"name\", \"email\"],\n     *   additionalProperties: false\n     * }\n```\n\n#### strict?\n\n```ts\noptional strict?: boolean;\n```\n\nWhether to enforce strict schema validation.\n\nWhen true (recommended), the model guarantees output will match the schema exactly.\nWhen false, the model will \"best effort\" match the schema.\n\nDefault: true (for providers that support it)\n\n##### See\n\nhttps://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/structured-outputs#strict-mode\n\n***\n\n### type\n\n```ts\ntype: \"json_object\" | \"json_schema\";\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:999](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L999)\n\nType of structured output.\n\n- \"json_object\": Forces the model to output valid JSON (any structure)\n- \"json_schema\": Validates output against a provided JSON Schema (strict structure)\n\n#### See\n\nhttps://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/chat/create#chat-create-response_format\n"}
